)","evidence":"The ADF established a stronghold at Suka na Mboka in Kebo chefferie (forest between Mambasa, Wamba and Watsa); FARDC clashed with them there on 30 April 2026 and conduct sweep operations. Over 10,000 people fled Kebo-Apodo, Andobi and Mahaa; villages are largely emptied and army-held positions face ADF incursions.","unit":"CD5309-watsa","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"adf","role":"contesting"}],"source_ids":[65,66,86,88,90,91]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Rural Watsa health zone (Kokoro, Dubele, Ngangazo, Monya, Gatanga, Moku, Maitulu, Arumbi, Dilolo etc.) and Akua/Nzopi villages","evidence":"No armed-group territorial control reported in northern and central Watsa; insecurity consists of armed robberies on artisanal mining sites. Moku received ADF displaced in 2026. Assigned to state police by default.","unit":"CD5309-watsa","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[65,89]},{"controller_id":"cod-fardc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"area_report","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Andobi chefferie: Mungbere (GRID3 'Salongo', Tangi) and Bakiri/Baitebi area","evidence":"Mungbere, capital of Andobi chefferie, is a reception point for displaced and the base for FARDC sweep operations against the ADF launched in 2026 with movement restrictions; ADF alerts and raids nearby (Apodo, March 2026) but the town remains government-held. FARDC presence in Mungbere predates 2026; the 2026 date marks the start of anti-ADF operations, not a change of controller.","unit":"CD5309-watsa","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-pnc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"adf","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[65,66,87]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"area_report","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Watsa-Durba urban area (Watsa centre, Durba/Kibali mine town and neighbourhoods Toyota, Bethanie, Doko, Durba, Gatanga)","evidence":"Territorial seat and Kibali gold mine hub, functioning normally (Kibali community programmes Sept 2026) and receiving people displaced by the ADF in mid-2026, i.e. state-held. Civil society complained in Jan 2026 of armed bandit attacks on nearby mining sites, which are criminal raids rather than territorial control.","unit":"CD5309-watsa","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[65,84,89]}],"sources":{"65":{"url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2026/07/14/actualite/securite/haut-uele-la-progression-des-adf-provoque-le-deplacement-de-plus-de-10","title":"Haut-Uele : la progression des ADF provoque le déplacement de plus de 10 000 civils vers Watsa et Wamba","publisher":"Radio Okapi","date":"2026-07-14"},"90":{"url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2026/08/31/actualite/securite/environ-10-000-deplaces-en-detresse-watsa-et-wamba","title":"Environ 10 000 déplacés en détresse à Watsa et Wamba","publisher":"Radio Okapi","date":"2026-08-31"},"66":{"url":"https://www.congoquotidien.com/2026/06/06/fardc-operations-adf-haut-uele/","title":"Haut-Uele : les FARDC ratissent Watsa contre les ADF et restreignent la circulation","publisher":"Congo Quotidien","date":"2026-06-06"},"86":{"url":"https://actu7.cd/2026/05/01/haut-uele-des-affrontements-entre-fardc-et-adf-signales-a-watsa/","title":"Haut-Uele : des affrontements entre FARDC et ADF signalés à Watsa","publisher":"Actu7.cd","date":"2026-05-01"},"88":{"url":"https://congorassure.com/securite/2026/03/31/haut-uele-pris-en-otages-par-les-adf-plus-de-100-civils-sauves-par-les-fardc","title":"Haut-Uélé : pris en otages par les ADF, plus de 100 civils sauvés par les FARDC","publisher":"Congo Rassure","date":"2026-03-31"},"91":{"url":"https://www.congo-press.com/provinces/haut-uele-eve-bazaiba-promet-un-retour-dans-la-dignite-aux-deplaces-de-suka-na-mboka/","title":"Haut-Uele : Eve Bazaiba promet un retour « dans la dignité » aux déplacés de Suka na Mboka","publisher":"MediaCongo Press","date":"2026-06-15"},"89":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202601160624.html","title":"La société civile fustige l'inertie des autorités face à la montée de l'insécurité à Watsa","publisher":"allAfrica / Radio Okapi","date":"2026-01-16"},"87":{"url":"https://www.mediacongo.net/publireportage-reportage-161998_haut_uele_calme_precaire_a_mungbere_apres_une_fausse_alerte_d_incursion_des_adf_a_apodo.html","title":"Haut-Uele : calme précaire à Mungbere après une fausse alerte d'incursion des ADF à Apodo","publisher":"Mediacongo","date":"2026-03"},"84":{"url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2026/09/28/actualite/societe/kibali-gold-distribue-62-000-plantules-de-cafeier-pour-relancer","title":"Kibali Gold distribue 62 000 plantules de caféier pour relancer l'agriculture à Faradje et Watsa (Haut-Uele)","publisher":"Radio Okapi","date":"2026-09-28"}},"units":{"CD5309-watsa":"Watsa territory (Haut-Uele) is mostly state-held: Watsa-Durba, the Kibali gold mine area, Gombari, Giro and Moku are run by police and administration with FARDC present, and northern/central areas see only banditry on mining sites. Since early 2026 the ADF/ISCAP has expanded north from Mambasa into the forests of the south, setting up a stronghold at Suka na Mboka in Kebo chefferie; FARDC clashed with them in April 2026 and run sweep operations. More than 10,000 people fled the Kebo-Apodo, Andobi and Mahaa chefferies toward Mungbere, Gombari, Watsa and Moku. The southern Apodo/Nepoko fringe is assessed as contested between FARDC and ADF; Mungbere is an FARDC operations hub."}}